From 388a0371d53ab9631db21f7970180b209de8dd01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 368/488] soh: name the 28 address-named symbols defined in
 z_demo_go.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 28 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Demo_Go/z_demo_go.c.

  * func_8097C8A8 -> DemoGo_PlayLandingSfx
    deduced, confidence HIGH: projects the Goron's position and plays
    NA_SE_EV_OBJECT_FALL there, for the two rolling Gorons only

  * func_8097C930 -> DemoGo_UpdateBlink
    deduced, confidence HIGH: counts the blink timer down, reseeds it, and
    clamps the eye texture index to 0-2

  * func_8097C9B8 -> DemoGo_PlayImpactSfx
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays NA_SE_EN_DODO_M_GND at the Goron's
    projected position

  * func_8097C9DC -> DemoGo_PlayFootstepSfx
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays NA_SE_EN_MORIBLIN_WALK on animation
    frames 12 and 25

  * func_8097CA30 -> DemoGo_UpdateBgCheck
    deduced, confidence HIGH: runs Actor_UpdateBgCheckInfo with the Goron's
    dimensions

  * func_8097CA78 -> DemoGo_SpawnLandingDust
    deduced, confidence HIGH: kicks up dust at the Goron's position with
    func_80033480 and plays the impact sound

  * func_8097CB0C -> DemoGo_MoveAlongCue
    deduced, confidence HIGH: lerps position between the cue's start and end
    points and takes the cue's yaw outright

  * func_8097CC08 -> DemoGo_WalkForward
    deduced, confidence HIGH: ramps speedXZ up to the kREG-tunable walk
    speed over eight frames and moves the actor

  * func_8097CCC0 -> DemoGo_MoveWithGravity
    deduced, confidence HIGH: moves the actor at its current speed with no
    speed change of its own

  * func_8097CCE0 -> DemoGo_TurnTowardCueYaw
    deduced, confidence HIGH: steps the Goron's yaw toward the cue's yaw at
    a capped rate instead of snapping to it

  * func_8097CDB0 -> DemoGo_IsCueAction
    deduced, confidence HIGH: true when this Goron's cue channel is live and
    sitting on the caller's action id

  * func_8097CE10 -> DemoGo_WaitForCutscene
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the action 0 step: advances straight to action
    1

  * func_8097CE20 -> DemoGo_WaitForRollCue
    deduced, confidence HIGH: on cue action 2, snaps to the cue, enables
    drawing and starts the roll

  * func_8097CE78 -> DemoGo_RollUntilCueEnds
    deduced, confidence HIGH: rides the cue until its end frame, then throws
    up landing dust and advances

  * func_8097CEEC -> DemoGo_WaitForUnfoldCue
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits for cue action 3 before unfolding

  * func_8097CF20 -> DemoGo_StartWalkAnim
    deduced, confidence HIGH: on the unfold animation finishing, loops
    gGoronAnim_0029A8 and resets the walk ramp

  * func_8097CF9C -> DemoGo_CountWalkRamp
    deduced, confidence HIGH: counts the eight-frame speed ramp out and
    advances to the full-speed walk

  * func_8097CFDC -> DemoGo_Action0
    deduced, confidence HIGH: action 0: nothing but the advance to action 1

  * func_8097CFFC -> DemoGo_Action1
    deduced, confidence HIGH: action 1: waits for the roll cue

  * func_8097D01C -> DemoGo_Action2
    deduced, confidence HIGH: action 2: rides the cue with bg checks until
    it ends

  * func_8097D058 -> DemoGo_Action3
    deduced, confidence HIGH: action 3: bg checks while waiting for the
    unfold cue

  * func_8097D088 -> DemoGo_Action4
    deduced, confidence HIGH: action 4: plays the unfold animation out and
    starts the walk

  * func_8097D0D0 -> DemoGo_Action5
    deduced, confidence HIGH: action 5: walks at ramping speed while turning
    toward the cue

  * func_8097D130 -> DemoGo_Action6
    deduced, confidence HIGH: action 6: the same walk at full speed

  * func_8097D290 -> DemoGo_DrawNothing
    deduced, confidence HIGH: draw config 0: draws nothing, used before the
